surname first name age qualifications  you complete these data regularly on the  internet but do you know that once you  enter them you lose control of them it's  impossible to delete them to recover  them or to stop them being sold to other  companies  the european parliament has at last  decided to resolve this problem by  protecting personal data on the internet  it wants to introduce more transparency  a right to be forgotten and also to set  boundaries on data transfers to third  parties  the european rules that are enforced  date backed in 1995 prehistoric times in  the digital world  if any company  doesn't matter if it's from the european  union or from somebody somewhere else  for example from the united states  doesn't respect the european data  protection rules then the data  protection authorities in europe  everywhere in every member state can  find the company with a sanction which  is up to five percent of a yearly  turnout of that company in addition to  companies restrictions meps also want to  limit data collection by national  authorities to within the framework of  criminal investigations but  the rules will be applicable throughout  the world as far as european citizens  are concerned regardless of whether the  data are stored outside the eu but the  united kingdom the netherlands and  ireland have expressed serious  reservations about the european  parliament's position which they judged  to be too punitive for small companies
 

